# Devlog #8 — Frontend improvements & new ideas

**2.9.2026 – 7.9.2026**

This time I spent around 4 hours working on SiteScope AI.

I mainly finished improving the frontend and tried to make it feel less AI-generated and more like my own design. While working on it, I came up with a few new ideas for the project, including new pages like **About** and **Thanks**, a simple footer and possibly different themes.

I also started working on hosting the backend. I found **Nest**, a free hosting service from Hack Club, and tried to deploy the backend there. It didn't go very well yet, but I learned a few things from it.

Later, I also worked on rewriting `main.py` so the Gemini API client follows the prompt from `prompt.md` more cleanly.

Overall, this was mostly a frontend and project-structure improvement phase, but I also came up with several new features I want to add later. 🚀
